@ 17.5.2 - Proto-Celtic to Middle Welsh
# citation: Dewrad & Pogostick Man, the latter citing Willis (David), “Old and Middle Welsh”
	kʷ > p
	V:[+long] > V / _#
	ei > e:[+long]
	st > s:[+long] (with some exceptions)
	ai > ɛ
	s > ∅ / V_V
	V > ə / _(C)#, also in proclitics
	s > ∅ / x_
	{au,eu,ou} > ∅
